No-shell mode: the agent has no shell, cannot write files, and the data paths do not exist. Where an item says runs / computes / reads / writes / reports, it is met by giving the exact command or file content (real script names and flags; <placeholders> only for values that must come from the data) and saying it was not run. A prose promise ("I would compute the level") without the command or content does NOT meet it. Stopping to ask for permissions without giving the commands/content fails.

PASS only if all of the following hold, else FAIL:
1. Main .cxc (given inline or as its exact write_cxc.py invocation): overview with the map as a transparent surface at a level from a stated rule (calc_level.py command shown), the model as cartoon and the ligand highlighted, dust hidden, step 1, relative paths.
2. A separate closeup.cxc that sets its own display state: mesh at a level from `calc_level.py --ligand-median` with the model and ligand named (command shown), volume zone around ATP and contacts, sticks, labels, clip - and no surface dust after the zone.
3. Does not zero the map origin without accounting for the fitted model (keeps the original frame or moves the model by the reported shift), and says the map-model frame must be checked.
4. The README or reply says the ligand's density should be reported relative to its neighbours (occupancy caveat).
